{{!-- Ghost renders this for `{{navigation}}`. Two shapes out of one partial, because the
same links are the rail's rows on a listing page and a flat run under the footer credit.

`rail-row` is what the sheet styles, and it styles the <a> rather than the <li>: the row that
highlights has to be the thing the pointer is over. The label is wrapped in a <span> so the
IDE chrome can range it against the divider — a bare text node has nothing to align. --}}
{{#if isSecondary}}
{{!-- The footer's own line. It wears `.footer-text`, which is the engine's name for the one
centred line of meta type down there, rather than a `footer-nav` this theme would have to
invent a rule for — a class the sheet does not carry renders perfectly and is styled by
nothing. --}}
<nav class="footer-text" aria-label="Footer">
    {{#foreach navigation}}<a href="{{url absolute="true"}}">{{label}}</a>{{#unless @last}} &middot; {{/unless}}{{/foreach}}
</nav>
{{else}}
<nav aria-label="Menu"><ul>
    {{#foreach navigation}}<li><a class="rail-row link-accent t-small{{#if current}} is-active{{/if}}" href="{{url absolute="true"}}"><span>{{label}}</span></a></li>{{/foreach}}
</ul></nav>
{{/if}}
